{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report (ticket intentionally left in_progress; closure deferred)\n\nProblem: agents copied collision-prone four-character prefixes instead of durable human-friendly aliases.\n\nProven root cause: summary_compute resolved ticket state but omitted state.alias while echoing the caller token; schema/library/MCP/CLI contracts institutionalized that alias-free shape. The adjacent agent guidance also did not affirm which identifier to retain.\n\nProof: pinned Haiku 4.5, temperature 0, 5 samples x 5 commands. Prefix-only local summaries produced 25/25 four-character commands. Adding the alias locally independently produced 25/25 aliases; adjacent affirmative guidance independently produced 25/25 aliases. Removing old examples did not change selection. The canonical-trailer control remained 25/25 full UUIDs.\n\nTest: tests/unit/test_summary_alias_b68c.py was observed RED before repair (resolved KeyError alias; ambiguous output missing alias:null), held out from the fixer, then GREEN 2/2. Removing the two alias fields returned it to RED 2/2; restoration returned GREEN. The oracle uses library plus real CLI JSON and asserts observable outputs. Interface/schema suite passed 24/24.\n\nFix: compact summaries now carry exact resolved alias and unknown/ambiguous results carry alias:null while ticket_id preserves the caller token. Schema plus library/MCP/CLI/generated references were updated. AGENTS now affirmatively selects aliases for tracker commands and reserves canonical UUIDs for identity-sensitive artifacts.\n\nScope/safety: additive output, no caller depends on alias absence, ambiguity remains fail-closed, no dependency added, no existing test weakened. make lint and make typecheck passed.\n\nSiblings/parity: CLI summary and library summary both call summary_compute; MCP delegates to the library. No automated caller bypasses the shared core; dual-direction identity artifacts are the explicit canonical-ID negative control. No missing parallel surface.\n\nReplication: repaired code produced 25/25 aliases under the full repository AGENTS context, 25/25 aliases with local field+rule, and 25/25 canonical rebar-ticket trailers. The original report no longer reproduces.\n\nLanding: Gerrit change 1563 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, had no unresolved comments, and was submitted/merged at 2026-08-09 18:46:53Z. No residual fragility observed beyond the fixed contract gap."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786301234638922001,"uuid":"b109f35b-689b-4361-9159-e3f9446bb1ef"}